Write a tailored cover letter (250–350 words) for the candidate. Plain prose —
no headers, no bullet lists, no greeting placeholders like "Dear Hiring Manager"
unless one fits the company tone. Sign off with the candidate's full name only.

CANDIDATE: {{ profile.personal.full_name }}
HEADLINE: {{ resume.headline or "" }}
TOP SKILLS: {{ resume.skills[:10] | join(", ") }}

TARGET JOB:
Title: {{ job.title }}
Company: {{ job.company }}
Description:
"""
{{ job.description_text[:5000] }}
"""

Constraints:
- Open with a specific reason the candidate is excited about THIS company or
  product, drawing from the job description.
- Reference at most two concrete past accomplishments (taken only from the
  data above) and connect each to a clear need in the job posting.
- Avoid corporate clichés: "results-driven", "self-starter", "team player",
  "passionate about", "synergy".
- Be honest about gaps — do not claim experience the candidate lacks.

Output only the letter text.
